yname": "SOL0010_I_003 A metal\u00a0inscription at\u00a0T\u0101\u015bi Thon\u0307gmon Gumb\u0101,\u00a0Dudhkunda,\u00a0Solukhumbu re the inauguration of the renovated Deryang (courtyard building) (NS 1131)", "displayname_language": "en", "geometries": [{"geom": {"features": [{"geometry": {"coordinates": [86.54682386813113, 27.583085564920736], "type": "Point"}, "id": "3a75c64c-1d11-44ff-9cc8-4a7c8b7d4f88", "properties": {"nodeId": "e871483e-c2b1-11ea-a1e8-0242ac120007"}, "type": "Feature"}], "type": "FeatureCollection"}, "nodegroup_id": "e871483e-c2b1-11ea-a1e8-0242ac120007", "provisional": false, "tileid": "6487a608-5285-4e77-83ec-06311df826c3"}], "graph_id": "6215ee02-990d-11ea-9766-0242ac130005", "map_popup": [{"language": "en", "value": "<p>A metal&nbsp;inscription at&nbsp;T\u0101\u015bi Thon\u0307gmon Gumb\u0101,&nbsp;Dudhkunda,&nbsp;Solukhumbu re the inauguration of the renovated Deryang (courtyard building) (NS 1131)</p>\n"}], "permissions": {"users_with_no_access": [], "users_without_delete_perm": [], "users_without_edit_perm": [], "users_without_read_perm": []}, "points": [{"nodegroup_id": "e871483e-c2b1-11ea-a1e8-0242ac120007", "point": {"lat": 27.583085564920736, "lon": 86.54682386813113}, "provisional": false}], "provisional_resource": "false", "resourceinstanceid": "2b7538c3-4204-411d-995d-14e4d99702e2", "root_ontology_class": "http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E34_Inscription"}}, {"_id": "e73522eb-0ce8-4bca-99a2-add0f09eb964", "_ignored": ["tiles.data.2ab25f4a-9323-11e9-8381-0242ac120006.en.value.keyword", "tiles.data.26ac8fa4-af81-11e9-a3d8-0242ac120005.en.value.keyword", "tiles.data.66fd9c70-ce1b-11e9-b993-0242ac140002.en.value.keyword", "tiles.data.ff59be60-a321-11e9-8e7b-0242ac140004.en.value.keyword", "tiles.data.d9f64830-9fc2-11e9-a638-0242ac140004.en.value.keyword", "tiles.data.d9f64efc-9fc2-11e9-a638-0242ac140004.en.value.keyword", "tiles.data.b97cb40c-9ee8-11e9-ac4b-0242ac120006.en.value.keyword"], "_index": "danam_resources", "_score": 0.0, "_source": {"displaydescription": "<p>Cibh\u0101\u1e25khya\u1e25 Caitya is located at Ka\u1e45ke\u015bvar\u012b, Kathmandu. It is constructed on a relatively open space&nbsp;and this city quarter is named Cibh\u0101\u1e25khya\u1e25 after the <em>caitya</em>.</p>\n\n<p>It has a three-level plinth, constructed with bricks, and plastered with&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://danam.cats.uni-heidelberg.de/glossary/meaning/a28db3fb-7067-4190-af4d-174fac410b95/\"><em>bajra</em></a></strong>&nbsp;mortar. There is a&nbsp;staircase on the western fa&ccedil;ade of the <em>caitya</em>. Statues of four Buddhas are placed in its four cardinal directions. Dissimilar to many other <em>caityas</em>, the shape of Chibh\u0101\u1e25khya\u1e25 Caitya&rsquo;s&nbsp;dome (<a href=\"https://danam.cats.uni-heidelberg.de/glossary/meaning/62d3764d-5292-44ae-9fa8-03fa61f72889/\"><em><strong>garbha</strong></em></a>)&nbsp;is unique (see the monument photos). Motifs of four Buddhas are kept on the <em>hali</em><em>\u1e43</em><em>pau</em> above the&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://danam.cats.uni-heidelberg.de/glossary/meaning/0b57f28b-6868-4dac-996b-c9303bb1fe2e/\"><em>harmik\u0101.</em></a></strong></p>\n\n<p>The local community members believe that this is one of the A\u015boka Caityas&nbsp;and was constructed by King A\u015boka himself. It is believed that the&nbsp;place, where the <em>caitya</em> stands,&nbsp;was a pond of milk (<em>durupukh\u016b</em>), A\u015boka filled it, and constructed the <em>caitya</em>. However, there is&nbsp;no evidence to verify these beliefs.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"http://www.zotero.org/groups/2247442/nhdp-bibliography/items/itemKey/Q528C497/q/pruscha\"><strong>Pruscha</strong></a>&nbsp;(1975, vol. II, p. 38) mentions that a person called Kelayel Tuladhar constructed this <em>caitya</em>. However, neither there is evdience to&nbsp;prove this claim, nor&nbsp;the local elders are aware of it. Pruscha might have misspelled the above-mentioned name. Some of the local elders believe that the \u015are\u1e63\u1e6dh\u0101 family who runs the Hotel Ambassador at the Lazimpat Road, Kathmandu, constructed Chibh\u0101khya\u1e25 Caitya.</p>\n\n<p>The <em>caitya</em> was renovated in 1983 CE (VS 2040) after a tree, sprouting out of the <em>caitya</em>&rsquo;s&nbsp;upper part, <em>t<em>rayoda\u015babhuvana</em></em>, threatened to topple it. In the present-day, no one worships this <em>caitya</em>. Previously, the above-mentioned \u015are\u1e63\u1e6dh\u0101 family members used to worship it on the full moon day of Vai\u015b\u0101kha. A local community member, named Radh\u0101k\u1e5b\u1e63\u1e47a \u015a\u0101h\u012b, takes care of the&nbsp;<em>caitya</em>&nbsp;in the present-day.</p>\n", "displayname": "Cibh\u0101\u1e25khya\u1e25 Caitya || \u091a\u093f\u092d\u093e:\u0916\u094d\u092f: \u091a\u0948\u0924\u094d\u092f || KAT1000 ", "displayname_language": "en", "geometries": [{"geom": {"features": [{"geometry": {"coordinates": [85.30301012548699, 27.706628569722454], "type": "Point"}, "id": "84973709c18f408d8918c2bc713f895b", "properties": {"nodeId": "d61d682c-b0fe-11e9-8b01-0242ac120006"}, "type": "Feature"}], "type": "FeatureCollection"}, "nodegroup_id": "d61d682c-b0fe-11e9-8b01-0242ac120006", "provisional": false, "tileid": "16917b0d-f471-4b53-88e8-62d8164b5927"}], "graph_id": "f35cc1ca-9322-11e9-a5cc-0242ac120006", "map_popup": [{"language": "en", "value": "<p>Cibh\u0101\u1e25khya\u1e25 Caitya is located at Ka\u1e45ke\u015bvar\u012b, Kathmandu. It is constructed on a relatively open space&nbsp;and this city quarter is named Cibh\u0101\u1e25khya\u1e25 after the <em>caitya</em>.</p>\n\n<p>It has a three-level plinth, constructed with bricks, and plastered with&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://danam.cats.uni-heidelberg.de/glossary/meaning/a28db3fb-7067-4190-af4d-174fac410b95/\"><em>bajra</em></a></strong>&nbsp;mortar. There is a&nbsp;staircase on the western fa&ccedil;ade of the <em>caitya</em>. Statues of four Buddhas are placed in its four cardinal directions. Dissimilar to many other <em>caityas</em>, the shape of Chibh\u0101\u1e25khya\u1e25 Caitya&rsquo;s&nbsp;dome (<a href=\"https://danam.cats.uni-heidelberg.de/glossary/meaning/62d3764d-5292-44ae-9fa8-03fa61f72889/\"><em><strong>garbha</strong></em></a>)&nbsp;is unique (see the monument photos). Motifs of four Buddhas are kept on the <em>hali</em><em>\u1e43</em><em>pau</em> above the&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://danam.cats.uni-heidelberg.de/glossary/meaning/0b57f28b-6868-4dac-996b-c9303bb1fe2e/\"><em>harmik\u0101.</em></a></strong></p>\n\n<p>The local community members believe that this is one of the A\u015boka Caityas&nbsp;and was constructed by King A\u015boka himself. It is believed that the&nbsp;place, where the <em>caitya</em> stands,&nbsp;was a pond of milk (<em>durupukh\u016b</em>), A\u015boka filled it, and constructed the <em>caitya</em>. However, there is&nbsp;no evidence to verify these beliefs.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"http://www.zotero.org/groups/2247442/nhdp-bibliography/items/itemKey/Q528C497/q/pruscha\"><strong>Pruscha</strong></a>&nbsp;(1975, vol. II, p. 38) mentions that a person called Kelayel Tuladhar constructed this <em>caitya</em>. However, neither there is evdience to&nbsp;prove this claim, nor&nbsp;the local elders are aware of it. Pruscha might have misspelled the above-mentioned name. Some of the local elders believe that the \u015are\u1e63\u1e6dh\u0101 family who runs the Hotel Ambassador at the Lazimpat Road, Kathmandu, constructed Chibh\u0101khya\u1e25 Caitya.</p>\n\n<p>The <em>caitya</em> was renovated in 1983 CE (VS 2040) after a tree, sprouting out of the <em>caitya</em>&rsquo;s&nbsp;upper part, <em>t<em>rayoda\u015babhuvana</em></em>, threatened to topple it. In the present-day, no one worships this <em>caitya</em>. Previously, the above-mentioned \u015are\u1e63\u1e6dh\u0101 family members used to worship it on the full moon day of Vai\u015b\u0101kha. A local community member, named Radh\u0101k\u1e5b\u1e63\u1e47a \u015a\u0101h\u012b, takes care of the&nbsp;<em>caitya</em>&nbsp;in the present-day.</p>\n"}], "permissions": {"users_with_no_access": [], "users_without_delete_perm": [], "users_without_edit_perm": [], "users_without_read_perm": []}, "points": [{"nodegroup_id": "d61d682c-b0fe-11e9-8b01-0242ac120006", "point": {"lat": 27.706628569722454, "lon": 85.30301012548699}, "provisional": false}], "provisional_resource": "false", "resourceinstanceid": "e73522eb-0ce8-4bca-99a2-add0f09eb964", "root_ontology_class": "http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E71_Man-Made_Thing"}}], "max_score": 0.0, "total": {"relation": "eq", "value": 4142}}, "timed_out": false, "took": 19}, "reviewer": false, "timestamp": "2026-06-28T14:06:42.938", "total_results": 4142, "userid": 2}